[184.227935, "o", "grep -n 'head of household' /app/statute.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[184.229427, "o", "204:(b) Definition of head of household\r\n394:        (B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or\r\n489:        (B) $275,000 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)),\r\n"]
[184.22945, "o", "491:        (C) $250,000 in the case of an individual who is not married and who is not a surviving spouse or head of household, and\r\n"]
[184.229654, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[184.229689, "o", "root@69c1033e4c34:/app# "]
[199.580733, "i", "sed -n '184,210p' /app/statute.txt\n"]
[199.58109, "o", "sed -n '184,210p' /app/statute.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[199.583143, "o", "(a) Definition of surviving spouse\r\n\r\n    (1) In general\r\n\r\n    For purposes of section 1, the term \"surviving spouse\" means a taxpayer-\r\n\r\n        (A) whose spouse died during either of the two years immediately preceding the taxable year, and\r\n\r\n        (B) who maintains as his home a household which constitutes for the taxable year the principal place of abode (as a member of such household) of a dependent (i) who (within the meaning of section 152) is a son, stepson, daughter, or stepdaughter of the taxpayer, and (ii) with respect to whom the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year under section 151.\r\n\r\n    For purposes of this paragraph, an individual shall be considered as maintaining a household only if over half of the cost of maintaining the household during the taxable year is furnished by such individual.\r\n\r\n    (2) Limitations\r\n\r\n"]
[199.583222, "o", "    Notwithstanding paragraph (1), for purposes of section 1 a taxpayer shall not be considered to be a surviving spouse-\r\n\r\n        (A) if the taxpayer has remarried at any time before the close of the taxable year, or\r\n\r\n        (B) unless, for the taxpayer's taxable year during which his spouse died, a joint return could have been made. A husband and wife may make a single return jointly of income taxes, even though one of the spouses has neither gross income nor deductions, except that no joint return shall be made if either the husband or wife at any time during the taxable year is a nonresident alien.\r\n\r\n(b) Definition of head of household\r\n\r\n    (1) In general\r\n\r\n    An individual shall be considered a head of a household if, and only if, such individual is not married at the close of his taxable year, is not a surviving spouse (as defined in subsection (a)), and either-\r\n\r\n        (A) maintains as his home a household which constitutes for more than one-half of such taxable year the principal place of"]
[199.58323, "o", " abode, as a member of such household, of-\r\n"]
[199.583761, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@69c1033e4c34:/app# "]
[200.089668, "i", "sed -n '204,230p' /app/statute.txt\n"]
[200.089998, "o", "sed -n '204,230p' /app/statute.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[200.091608, "o", "(b) Definition of head of household\r\n\r\n    (1) In general\r\n\r\n    An individual shall be considered a head of a household if, and only if, such individual is not married at the close of his taxable year, is not a surviving spouse (as defined in subsection (a)), and either-\r\n\r\n        (A) maintains as his home a household which constitutes for more than one-half of such taxable year the principal place of abode, as a member of such household, of-\r\n\r\n            (i) a qualifying child of the individual (as defined in section 152(c)), but not if such child-\r\n\r\n                (I) is married at the close of the taxpayer's taxable year, and\r\n\r\n                (II) is not a dependent of such individual by reason of section 152(b)(2) or\r\n\r\n"]
[200.091643, "o", "            (ii) any other person who is a dependent of the taxpayer, if the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year for such person under section 151, or\r\n\r\n        (B) maintains a household which constitutes for such taxable year the principal place of abode of the father or mother of the taxpayer, if the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year for such father or mother under section 151.\r\n\r\n    For purposes of this paragraph, an individual shall be considered as maintaining a household only if over half of the cost of maintaining the household during the taxable year is furnished by such individual.\r\n\r\n    (2) Determination of status\r\n\r\n    Notwithstanding paragraph (1),\r\n"]
[200.09178, "o", "\r\n        (A) an individual who is legally separated from his spouse under a decree of divorce or of separate maintenance shall not be considered as married;\r\n\r\n        (B) a taxpayer shall be considered as not married at the close of his taxable year if at any time during the taxable year his spouse is a nonresident alien; and\r\n"]
[200.091951, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[200.091971, "o", "root@69c1033e4c34:/app# "]
[225.425666, "i", "grep -n 'qualifying relative\\|qualifying child\\|section 152' /app/statute.txt | head -20\n"]
[225.426003, "o", "grep -n 'qualifying relative\\|qualifying child\\|section 152' /app/statute.txt | head -20\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[225.428254, "o", "64:An exemption of the exemption amount for each individual who is a dependent (as defined in section 152) of the taxpayer for the taxable year.\r\n101:    (1) a qualifying child, or\r\n103:    (2) a qualifying relative.\r\n123:    The term \"qualifying child\" means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual-\r\n143:    For purposes of paragraph (1)(C), an individual meets the requirements of this paragraph if such individual is younger than the taxpayer claiming such individual as a qualifying child and is less than 25 years old at the end of the taxable year.\r\n151:    The term \"qualifying relative\" means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual-\r\n157:        (D) who is not a qualifying child of such taxpayer or of any other taxpayer for any taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which such taxable year begins.\r\n192:        (B) who maintains as his home a household which constitutes for the taxable year the principal place of abode (as a member of such household"]
[225.428306, "o", ") of a dependent (i) who (within the meaning of section 152) is a son, stepson, daughter, or stepdaughter of the taxpayer, and (ii) with respect to whom the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year under section 151.\r\n212:            (i) a qualifying child of the individual (as defined in section 152(c)), but not if such child-\r\n216:                (II) is not a dependent of such individual by reason of section 152(b)(2) or\r\n240:        (B) by reason of an individual who would not be a dependent for the taxable year but for subparagraph (H) of section 152(d)(2).\r\n"]
[225.428566, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
