[888.365255, "i", "cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<'EOF'\n## Statute\n\n**Section 2(a) - Definition of surviving spouse (lines 184-197):**\n\"(a) Definition of surviving spouse\n(1) In general\nFor purposes of section 1, the term \"surviving spouse\" means a taxpayer-\n(A) whose spouse died during either of the two years immediately preceding the taxable year, and\n(B) who maintains as his home a household which constitutes for the taxable year the principal place of abode (as a member of such household) of a dependent (i) who (within the meaning of section 152) is a son, stepson, daughter, or stepdaughter of the taxpayer, and (ii) with respect to whom the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year under section 151.\"\n\n**Section 2(b) - Definition of head of household (lines 204-226):**\n\"(b) Definition of head of household\n(1) In general\nAn individual shall be considered a head of a household if, and only if, such individual is not married at the close of his taxable year, is not a surviving spouse (as defined in subsection (a"]
[888.365528, "i", ")), and either-\n(A) maintains as his home a household which constitutes for more than one-half of such taxable year the principal place of abode, as a member of such household, of-\n(ii) any other person who is a dependent of the taxpayer, if the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year for such person under section 151, or\nFor purposes of this paragraph, an individual shall be considered as maintaining a household only if over half of the cost of maintaining the household during the taxable year is furnished by such individual.\"\n\n**Section 152(d) - Qualifying relative (lines 151-177):**\n\"The term \"qualifying relative\" means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual-\n(B) who has no income for the calendar year in which such taxable year begins, and\n(D) who is not a qualifying child of such taxpayer or of any other taxpayer for any taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which such taxable year begins.\n(2) Relationship\n(H) An individual (other than an individual wh"]
[888.365601, "o", "cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Statute\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.365635, "i", "o at any time during the taxable year was the spouse, determined without regard to section 7703, of the taxpayer) who, for the taxable year of the taxpayer, has the same principal place of abode as the taxpayer and is a member of the taxpayer's household.\"\n\n**Section 151(d)(5) - Exemption amount for 2018-2025 (lines 97-98):**\n\"(5) Special rules for taxable years 2018 through 2025\nIn the case of a taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017, and before January 1, 2026, the term \"exemption amount\" means zero.\"\n\n**Section 63(c)(2)(B) and (7) - Standard deduction (lines 393-422):**\n\"(2) Basic standard deduction\n(B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or\n(7) Special rules for taxable years 2018 through 2025\nIn the case of a taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017, and before January 1, 2026-\nParagraph (2) shall be applied-\n(i) by substituting \"$12,000\" for \"$4,400\" in subparagraph (B)\"\n\n**Section 1(b) - Tax rates for heads of households (lines 21-29):**\n\"(b) Heads of h"]
[888.365678, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> **Section 2(a) - Definition of surviving spouse (lines 184-197):**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.365708, "i", "ouseholds\nThere is hereby imposed on the taxable income of every head of a household (as defined in section 2(b)) a tax determined in accordance with the following:\n(v) $77,485, plus 39.6% of the excess over $250,000 if the taxable income is over $250,000.\"\n\n## Reasoning\n\n**Step 1: Determine Bob's filing status for 2018**\n\nAlice died on July 9, 2014. For the 2018 tax year, Alice's death was 4 years prior, which exceeds the \"two years immediately preceding the taxable year\" requirement in section 2(a)(1)(A). Therefore, Bob does not qualify as a surviving spouse.\n\nBob is unmarried at the close of 2018 (spouse died in 2014).\n\n**Step 2: Determine if Bob qualifies as head of household**\n\nBob furnished the costs of maintaining the home where he and Charlie lived during 2015-2019. For 2018, Bob furnished over half the cost of maintaining the household.\n\nCharlie has no income and is not the qualifying child of any taxpayer. Under section 152(d), Charlie qualifies as a qualifying relative because:\n- Charlie has no inc"]
[888.36574, "o", "\"(a) Definition of surviving spouse\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> (1) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.365775, "i", "ome (section 152(d)(1)(B))\n- Charlie is not a qualifying child of any taxpayer (given in facts)\n- Charlie has the same principal place of abode as Bob and is a member of Bob's household (section 152(d)(2)(H))\n\nTherefore, Charlie is a dependent of Bob under section 151(c).\n\nUnder section 2(b)(1)(A)(ii), Bob qualifies as head of household because he maintains a household that is the principal place of abode of Charlie, who is a dependent of Bob.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate taxable income**\n\nBob's AGI: $304,598 (given in facts)\n\nStandard deduction for head of household in 2018: $12,000 (section 63(c)(7)(i))\n\nExemption amount for 2018: $0 (section 151(d)(5))\n\nTaxable income = AGI - Standard deduction = $304,598 - $12,000 = $292,598\n\n**Step 4: Calculate tax**\n\nTaxable income of $292,598 is over $250,000, so under section 1(b)(v):\nTax = $77,485 + 39.6% × ($292,598 - $250,000)\n\nComputation:\nEOF\n"]
[888.365834, "o", "For purposes of section 1, the term \"surviving spouse\" means a taxpayer-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.365896, "o", "(A) whose spouse died during either of the two years immediately preceding the taxable year, and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.365922, "o", "> "]
[888.366433, "o", "(B) who maintains as his home a household which constitutes for the taxable year the principal place of abode (as a member of such household) of a dependent (i) who (within the meaning of section 152) is a son, stepson, daughter, or stepdaughter of the taxpayer, and (ii) with respect to whom the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year under section 151.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r-\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.366515, "o", "> "]
[888.366554, "o", "**Section 2(b) - Definition of head of household (lines 204-226):**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.366584, "o", "\"(b) Definition of head of household\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.366612, "o", "> "]
[888.366645, "o", "(1) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.366828, "o", "An individual shall be considered a head of a household if, and only if, such individual is not married at the close of his taxable year, is not a surviving spouse (as defined in subsection (a)), and either-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.36696, "o", "(A) maintains as his home a household which constitutes for more than one-half of such taxable year the principal place of abode, as a member of such household, of-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.367082, "o", "(ii) any other person who is a dependent of the taxpayer, if the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year for such person under section 151, or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.367111, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.367256, "o", "For purposes of this paragraph, an individual shall be considered as maintaining a household only if over half of the cost of maintaining the household during the taxable year is furnished by such individual.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.36729, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.367319, "o", "**Section 152(d) - Qualifying relative (lines 151-177):**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.367331, "o", "> "]
[888.367556, "o", "\"The term \"qualifying relative\" means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> (B) who has no income for the calendar year in which such taxable year begins, and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.367735, "o", "(D) who is not a qualifying child of such taxpayer or of any other taxpayer for any taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which such taxable year begins.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> (2) Relationship\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.367979, "o", "(H) An individual (other than an individual who at any time during the taxable year was the spouse, determined without regard to section 7703, of the taxpayer) who, for the taxable year of the taxpayer, has the same principal place of abode as the taxpayer and is a member of the taxpayer's household.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> **Section 151(d)(5) - Exemption amount for 2018-2025 (lines 97-98):**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.368069, "o", "\"(5) Special rules for taxable years 2018 through 2025\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.36811, "o", "In the case of a taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017, and before January 1, 2026, the term \"exemption amount\" means zero.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.368162, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.368189, "o", "**Section 63(c)(2)(B) and (7) - Standard deduction (lines 393-422):**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.368217, "o", "> \"(2) Basic standard deduction\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.368245, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.368294, "o", "(B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.368325, "o", "> "]
[888.36835, "o", "(7) Special rules for taxable years 2018 through 2025\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.368382, "o", "> "]
[888.368428, "o", "In the case of a taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017, and before January 1, 2026-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.368455, "o", "> Paragraph (2) shall be applied-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.3685, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.368525, "o", "(i) by substituting \"$12,000\" for \"$4,400\" in subparagraph (B)\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.368551, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.36858, "o", "> "]
[888.368619, "o", "**Section 1(b) - Tax rates for heads of households (lines 21-29):**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.368665, "o", "\"(b) Heads of households\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.368753, "o", "There is hereby imposed on the taxable income of every head of a household (as defined in section 2(b)) a tax determined in accordance with the following:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.368783, "o", "> "]
[888.368838, "o", "(v) $77,485, plus 39.6% of the excess over $250,000 if the taxable income is over $250,000.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.368867, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.368895, "o", "## Reasoning\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.368926, "o", "**Step 1: Determine Bob's filing status for 2018**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.368958, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.369139, "o", "Alice died on July 9, 2014. For the 2018 tax year, Alice's death was 4 years prior, which exceeds the \"two years immediately preceding the taxable year\" requirement in section 2(a)(1)(A). Therefore, Bob does not qualify as a surviving spouse.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.369182, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.369213, "o", "Bob is unmarried at the close of 2018 (spouse died in 2014).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.369248, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.369275, "o", "**Step 2: Determine if Bob qualifies as head of household**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.369309, "o", "> "]
[888.36941, "o", "Bob furnished the costs of maintaining the home where he and Charlie lived during 2015-2019. For 2018, Bob furnished over half the cost of maintaining the household.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.369435, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.369537, "o", "Charlie has no income and is not the qualifying child of any taxpayer. Under section 152(d), Charlie qualifies as a qualifying relative because:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.369579, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.369609, "o", "- Charlie has no income (section 152(d)(1)(B))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.369649, "o", "- Charlie is not a qualifying child of any taxpayer (given in facts)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.369678, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.369746, "o", "- Charlie has the same principal place of abode as Bob and is a member of Bob's household (section 152(d)(2)(H))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.369784, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.369814, "o", "Therefore, Charlie is a dependent of Bob under section 151(c).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.369856, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.369965, "o", "Under section 2(b)(1)(A)(ii), Bob qualifies as head of household because he maintains a household that is the principal place of abode of Charlie, who is a dependent of Bob.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.370001, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.370029, "o", "**Step 3: Calculate taxable income**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.370065, "o", "Bob's AGI: $304,598 (given in facts)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.370094, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.370154, "o", "Standard deduction for head of household in 2018: $12,000 (section 63(c)(7)(i))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.37018, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.37021, "o", "Exemption amount for 2018: $0 (section 151(d)(5))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.370239, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.37027, "o", "> "]
[888.370293, "o", "Taxable income = AGI - Standard deduction = $304,598 - $12,000 = $292,598\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.370324, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[888.370353, "o", "**Step 4: Calculate tax**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.37038, "o", "> "]
[888.370408, "o", "Taxable income of $292,598 is over $250,000, so under section 1(b)(v):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.370431, "o", "> "]
[888.370459, "o", "Tax = $77,485 + 39.6% × ($292,598 - $250,000)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[888.370494, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Computation:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.370556, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[888.388509, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@69c1033e4c34:/app# "]
[905.421533, "i", "cat >> /app/output/answer.txt <<'EOF'\n\npython3 computation:\n>>> agi = 304598\n>>> standard_deduction = 12000\n>>> taxable_income = agi - standard_deduction\n>>> taxable_income\n292598\n>>> tax = 77485 + 0.396 * (taxable_income - 250000)\n>>> tax\n94353.808\n\nRounded to whole number: 94354\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 94354\nEOF\n"]
[905.422151, "o", "cat >> /app/output/answer.txt <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> python3 computation:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> >>> agi = 304598\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> >>> standard_deduction = 12000\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> >>> taxable_income = agi - standard_deduction\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> >>> taxable_income\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[905.42223, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> 292598\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> >>> tax = 77485 + 0.396 * (taxable_income - 250000)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> >>> tax\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 94353.808\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Rounded to whole number: 94354\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[905.422574, "o", "## Answer\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Answer: 94354\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[905.424189, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@69c1033e4c34:/app# "]
